{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Systemic Game.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Systemic Game.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"systemic game systemic game","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Systemic Game.md","fileName":"Systemic Game.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Systemic Game","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Emergent Game Narrative]] [[Emergent Systems]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Emergent Game Narrative","Emergent Systems","Play Space","Content-Driven Game","Emergent Story","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Systemic Game.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Systemic Game.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"systemic game systemic game","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Systemic Game.md","fileName":"Systemic Game.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Systemic Game","heading":"Systemic Game","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A systemic game derives much of its gameplay from interacting feedback loops rather than from a single authored sequence. The systems generate a [[Play Space]] in which players can pursue many paths and produce emergent outcomes.\n\nSystemic structure supports replayability and mastery because the same parts can combine differently across play. It does not eliminate content; it uses content as material within systems rather than relying on a continuous [[Content-Driven Game|content treadmill]].\n\nWhen relationships among verbs and objects create many possible situations, players can discover strategies and produce [[Emergent Story|stories]] the creator did not script. The system still bounds those outcomes, but it facilitates rather than fully authors their sequence.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Emergent Game Narrative","Emergent Systems","Play Space","Content-Driven Game","Emergent Story","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Systemic Game.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Systemic Game.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"systemic game systemic game","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Systemic Game.md","fileName":"Systemic Game.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Systemic Game","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[advancedgamedesign.pdf]]\n[[agamedesignvocabulary.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Emergent Game Narrative","Emergent Systems","Play Space","Content-Driven Game","Emergent Story","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}